        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Eagle Valley in Enniskerry\n\nWell situated in a quiet cul-de-sac in the highly regarded Eagle Valley, above the village of Enniskerry adjacent to The Powerscourt Estate. 39 Eagle Valley is a beautifully presented five-bedroom detached family residence extending to approximately 293 sq.m (3,154 sq.ft), offering exceptionally spacious accommodation, elegant interiors and beautifully landscaped private gardens.\n\nPresented in excellent condition throughout, this impressive home has been thoughtfully upgraded and enhanced over the years to create a wonderful balance between generous family living and stylish entertaining spaces. \n\nThe property is entered through a bright and welcoming entrance hall, setting the tone for the quality and care evident throughout. To the front of the house are two beautifully proportioned reception rooms, each featuring an attractive fireplace and large windows that flood the rooms with natural light. These versatile spaces provide the perfect setting for formal entertaining, a family television room, home office or playroom. \n\nTo the rear lies the true heart of the home, an outstanding open-plan kitchen and breakfast room featuring a large central island, extensive fitted cabinetry and quality stone worktops. This superb space flows seamlessly into a generous dining area, creating an ideal setting for both family life and entertaining. Beyond, a magnificent family room extension with vaulted ceilings, rooflights and a feature stove provides an exceptional living space overlooking the gardens. Bathed in natural light throughout the day, this room offers a wonderful connection to the outdoors and serves as a relaxing retreat for the whole family. \n\nA guest WC and additional storage complete the ground-floor accommodation. \n\nUpstairs, a spacious landing leads to five well-proportioned bedrooms. The principal suite enjoys the benefit of a private ensuite bathroom together with a walk-in wardrobe, creating a luxurious and peaceful retreat. Two further bedrooms are connected via a Jack-and-Jill ensuite, while the remaining bedrooms are served by the family bathroom, ensuring excellent accommodation for growing families and visiting guests alike. \n\nA particular feature of this home is the converted attic level, providing two substantial and highly versatile rooms currently used as a gym, hobby room and laundry area. These bright, adaptable spaces offer excellent flexibility for a range of uses including home working, fitness, recreation, storage or additional family accommodation, subject to a purchaser's individual requirements. \n\nOutside, the property is surrounded by mature and meticulously maintained gardens enjoying a high degree of privacy and sunny back garden also with a substantial front garden with ample parking. Beautiful planting, established trees and colourful flower beds create a tranquil setting, while paved patio areas provide the perfect space for outdoor dining and entertaining during the warmer months. \n\nEagle Valley represents a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial family home in one of Enniskerry's most sought-after residential developments. Combining spacious accommodation, elegant interiors, superb entertaining spaces and a prime village location, this exceptional property offers the perfect balance of countryside tranquillity and convenient access to Dublin. \n\nKey Features \n\n- Exceptional detached five-bedroom family residence \n\n- Approx. 293 sq.m / 3,154 sq.ft of accommodation \n\n- Three reception rooms plus spectacular family room extension \n\n- Contemporary kitchen with large central island and adjoining dining area \n\n- Guest WC \n\n- Principal bedroom with ensuite bathroom and walk-in wardrobe \n\n- Jack-and-Jill ensuite serving two bedrooms \n\n- Converted attic level with two versatile rooms \n\n- Beautifully landscaped private gardens with ample parking\n\n- Exclusive and highly desirable residential setting \n\n- Within walking distance of Enniskerry Village \n\n- Close to Powerscourt Estate, excellent schools and major transport routes"
      },
